' ============================================================
' greeter.dbas — Helper file
' ============================================================
' This file is INCLUDEd by FirstProgram.dbas. When DBasic sees
' INCLUDE "greeter.dbas", it acts as if the contents of THIS
' file were copy-pasted right there. So the SUB defined here
' becomes usable in the main program.
' ============================================================

' SayHello prints a friendly greeting using the name we're given.
' The semicolons (;) glue the pieces together so they end up on
' one line.
SUB SayHello(name AS STRING)
    PRINT "Hello, "; name; "! Welcome to DBasic."
END SUB
